            <ArticleTitle>Coronary-pulmonary artery fistula with anomalous vessels arising from the right coronary sinus detected by 64-MDCT.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1893-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a case of aneurysmal coronary-pulmonary artery fistula and a communicating anomalous vessel arising from the right coronary sinus that was clearly demonstrated by 64-multidetector row computed tomography (MDCT). MDCT angiography was more useful than cardiac catheterization for planning the surgical strategy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
